[ti:Secret Room]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:1984s.text - Rectified]
[length:03:25.90]

[00:04.82]Shh... shh... no screen up here
[00:08.04]Just the clock... and her, singing
[00:13.85]Narrow scarlet sash tight around her waist
[00:21.30]She moves like danger wrapped in perfect grace
[00:29.31]I hated her, I want her, I fear her the most
[00:32.94]Three words on a scrap of paper... and I know
[00:37.40]Up the stairs above the junk shop door
[00:41.14]An old clock ticking like it did before
[00:44.52]We are the dead... we are the dead
[00:52.37]But for one stolen hour we are alive instead
[01:01.41]They can watch the streets but they can't watch inside
[01:08.43]For one brief moment the Party has no eyes
[01:16.72]Paperweight of coral, a whole world under glass
[01:20.53]A woman hangs the washing, singing as the hours pass
[01:24.61]Oranges and lemons, say the bells of St Clement's
[01:28.34]A heavy book, no name, no title, on my knees
[01:31.78]It tells me what I know... I fall asleep before the why
[01:40.40]Up the stairs where no one ever goes
[01:44.18]An old clock ticking... only the clock knows
[01:47.78]No screens, no eyes... nothing left unsaid
[01:55.35]But for one stolen hour we are alive instead
[02:02.94]Secret room... no screens... just us
[02:11.39]And the picture on the wall holds its breath for us
[02:18.94]But for one stolen hour we are alive instead
[02:27.01]For one brief moment... for one brief moment
[02:34.79]We are the dead
[02:37.16]We are the dead
[02:38.82]You are the dead
[02:40.82]Stay where you are
[02:42.44]This room was never yours
[02:46.18]Instrumental
[02:52.18]I wrote it as a warning, not as an instruction manual
[02:56.64]A rented room. A woman. A song from the yard below
[03:01.48]That was all they had, and it was enough to hang them
[03:05.04]What comes next is not a fight. It's a cure
[03:08.54]They won't break him. They'll teach him to be grateful
[03:12.39]Don't let it happen. It depends on you
[03:14.69]
